Let me formally define each component:

3.2.1 Witness Nodes

A Witness Node W\_i is defined as a tuple (PK\_i, SK\_i, L\_i, R\_i)
where: ●\hspace{0pt} PK\_i, SK\_i: Key pair for digital signatures\\
●\hspace{0pt} L\_i: Current location coordinates\\
●\hspace{0pt} R\_i: Reputation score

Each Witness Node maintains:\\
1.\hspace{0pt} Network state including peer list\\
2.\hspace{0pt} Local verification history\\
3.\hspace{0pt} Cryptographic parameters

\emph{Definition 3.2.1 (Valid Witness):} A witness W\_i is considered
valid if: ●\hspace{0pt} R\_i \textgreater{} threshold\_R\\
●\hspace{0pt} \textbar Active\_time\textbar{} \textgreater{}
threshold\_T\\
●\hspace{0pt} Verify(cert\_i, CA\_pk) = 1

\emph{Security Properties:}\\
1.\hspace{0pt} Byzantine fault tolerance up to f \textless{} n/2
malicious witnesses 2.\hspace{0pt} Verifiable reputation scores\\
3.\hspace{0pt} Location privacy through ZK proofs

3.2.2 PPR Generation

A Proximity Proof Request (PPR) is generated as follows:

