\begin{quote}
\emph{Theorem 3.3 (Selection Security):} The witness selection algorithm
achieves:\\
1.\hspace{0pt} Byzantine fault tolerance up to f \textless{} n/2
malicious nodes\\
2.\hspace{0pt} Uniform distribution of honest witnesses\\
3.\hspace{0pt} Reputation-weighted selection probability\\
\emph{Proof:} Let A be any PPT adversary controlling f nodes. The
probability of controlling k selected witnesses is:\\
P(success) = ∏ᵢ(f\_i/n\_i) ≤ (f/n)ᵏ ≤ negl(λ)\\
Where f\_i, n\_i represent remaining malicious and total nodes at step
i.

