\emph{Theorem 3.4 (ZKRP Security):} The Location ZKRP achieves:
●\hspace{0pt} Perfect Completeness\\
●\hspace{0pt} Special Soundness\\
●\hspace{0pt} Special Honest-Verifier Zero-Knowledge

\emph{Proof:} Let me prove each property:\\
1.\hspace{0pt} \emph{Perfect Completeness:}\hspace{0pt}\\
For any l ∈ {[}a,b{]}, honest prover P, and honest verifier
V:\hspace{0pt}\\
Pr{[}⟨P(l,r),V⟩ = 1{]} = 1\\
2.\hspace{0pt} \emph{Special Soundness:} Given accepting transcripts
(a,e₁,z₁) and (a,e₂,z₂) with e₁ ≠ e₂,\hspace{0pt} one can efficiently
extract a witness l ∈ {[}a,b{]}.

3.\hspace{0pt} \emph{Special HVZK:} There exists a simulator S such
that:\hspace{0pt}\\
\{S(pp,{[}a,b{]})\} ≈\_c \{⟨P(l,r),V⟩\}

The full proof appears in \uline{Appendix A.5}.

3.3.5 Proximity Proof Response Generation

Each witness W\_i generates a proof response PPRs as follows:

\emph{PPRs Generation Algorithm:}
\end{quote}

