\begin{quote}
5. Enhanced Privacy Mechanisms

\textbf{5.1 Differential Privacy for Location Data}

I introduce a novel differential privacy mechanism specifically designed
for location proofs:\\
\emph{Definition 5.1 (Location Differential Privacy):} A mechanism M
satisfies (ε,δ)-location privacy if for all neighboring locations l₁,l₂
and all sets S:\\
Pr{[}M(l₁) ∈ S{]} ≤ exp(ε) · Pr{[}M(l₂) ∈ S{]} + δ\\
\emph{Theorem 5.1:} The following noise addition mechanism achieves
(ε,0)-location privacy:
\end{quote}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 0\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 0\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
AddNoise(l, ε) → l\textquotesingle:\\
1. Sample η ∼ Laplace(Δf/ε)\\
where Δf is location sensitivity 2. Return l\textquotesingle{} = l + η
\end{quote}\strut
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}\strut
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\begin{quote}
\emph{Proof:} Let me show that for any neighboring locations:\\
Privacy Loss = ln(Pr{[}M(l₁)=z{]}/Pr{[}M(l₂)=z{]})\\
=
ln(exp(-\textbar z-l₁\textbar·ε/Δf)/exp(-\textbar z-l₂\textbar·ε/Δf))\\
= (\textbar z-l₂\textbar{} - \textbar z-l₁\textbar)·ε/Δf ≤ ε

\textbf{5.2 k-Anonymity Through Witness Selection}

I propose a novel witness selection algorithm that guarantees
k-anonymity:\\
\emph{Definition 5.2 (k-Anonymous Witness Selection):} A selection
mechanism that ensures each proof is indistinguishable from at least k-1
other proofs.

\emph{Algorithm: k-Anonymous Selection}
\end{quote}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 0\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 0\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
SelectKAnonymousWitnesses(W, k) → W\textquotesingle:\\
1. Cluster witnesses into groups G\_i of size ≥ k\\
2. Select group G\_j with probability ∝ min(\textbar G\_j\textbar, 2k)
3. Return random subset of G\_j
\end{quote}\strut
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}\strut
\end{minipage} \\
